ok   gen writes the precision bound of every decimal column that declares one
ok   save stores a REAL rounded to the scale, and the read is the same decimal
ok   a whole value is stored as an INTEGER and read as a Float
ok   nil and an empty field are NULL, never 0.0; text that is not a number is 0.0
ok   rounding is half away from zero on the decimal digits
ok   rounding is idempotent, also past 15 significant digits
ok   the attribute keeps what was assigned; the row and a reload have the rounded value
ok   every value of the declared precision reads back as the decimal that was written
ok   15 significant digits round-trip through Cast and SQLite, 16 do not
ok   save refuses a value outside the declared precision, Infinity and NaN
ok   a value that rounds up to the bound is stored
ok   update, update_columns and update_all round as save does
ok   insert_all and upsert_all round as save does
ok   the writers without validations store a value outside the range
ok   sum_float, average, minimum_float and maximum_float answer Floats
ok   a rounded sum of many prices equals the sum of their cents
ok   to_json writes the decimal as a JSON number
ok   minor units in an integer column are exact: parse, store, sum, display
